      "writtenOn": "2022-10-27T20:32:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Out of scope, but it bugs me how module interfaces gradually bubble their way up into this file when they become useful to host commands. I\u0027m assuming you did this because usb_pd.h already includes ec_commands.h, and there was a dependency loop. Particularly as we move to Zephyr, we should figure out a way to avoid/mitigate this situation.\n\nIt makes sense to me that ec_commands.h would include various other module header files, since it cuts across features. Maybe, to avoid other header files including ec_commands.h, we could make a habit of defining host commands in their own libraries that include both ec_commands.h and the relevant module header. Additional advantages of that approach would be simplifying our use of host-command Kconfigs and forcing us to implement host commands in terms of well defined library interfaces.",
      "revId": "e0df2bb1fed20d42df92eb663e352870c02ea1ab",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
